Owner decision OD-DLP002-R1. This is a NEW governance authorization for TECP-DLP-002-DISPOSABLE-TASK-CLAIM-LEASE-BINDING. TECP-DLP-001 remains CLOSED / FROZEN / VERIFIED via PR #232 implementation and PR #233 closeout. DLP-001 historical evidence, residual F2/F3/F4 owner acceptance, and NON_OPERATIONAL proof status are preserved and are not reopened. No DLP-002 implementation, frozen-boundary edit, dependency install or database execution is authorized until this governance PR is separately owner-approved and merged. While this PR is unmerged, TECP_DLP002_EFFECTIVE_BEFORE_MERGE = NO and TECP_IMPLEMENTATION_AUTHORIZED remains NO / UNTIL_THIS_GOVERNANCE_PR_MERGES at the Snapshot layer.

Owner decision OD-DLP002-R2. Architecture Option C is mandatory. Nested reuse of the self-managing acquireWriteLease / renewWriteLease / releaseWriteLease transaction boundary inside an outer Task/Claim transaction is UNSAFE and forbidden. A new adapter that duplicates the WRITE lease algorithm is forbidden. After merge, implementation may apply a narrow frozen-boundary exception ONLY to the two existing paths tecp-persistence/src/writeLeaseRepository.js and tecp-persistence/test/writeLeaseRepository.test.js, limited to additive caller-owned transaction entry points (or equivalent manageTransaction=false mechanism) plus regression tests. Existing public acquireWriteLease, renewWriteLease, releaseWriteLease and validateWriteLease behavior for existing callers MUST remain unchanged.

Owner decision OD-DLP002-R3. Transaction ownership contract: in-transaction lease mutation APIs MUST NOT issue BEGIN, COMMIT or ROLLBACK. Callers MUST prove an authorized open transaction on the injected client before invoking in-transaction lease mutations; do not assume an arbitrary PostgreSQL client is already inside a transaction. Task, Claim and Lease mutations for one composition MUST share exactly one outer transaction. Any DENY, throw or failure during composition MUST ROLLBACK all participating writes. Fencing-epoch monotonicity, idempotency, CAS expected_version, governance-revision enforcement and fail-closed DB error handling from DLP-001 MUST be preserved.

Owner decision OD-DLP002-R4. After this governance PR merges, implementation is limited to the FIVE exact paths in AUTHORIZED_FILE_SCOPE. New composition files are tecp-persistence/src/taskClaimLeaseRepository.js, tecp-persistence/test/disposableTaskClaimLeaseSchema.sql and tecp-persistence/test/taskClaimLeaseRepository.test.js. The other four frozen DLP-001 files (package.json, package-lock.json, disposableSchema.sql, disposablePgHarness.js) remain protected and must not be modified. No new npm dependencies. Reuse existing pinned pg@8.16.3 only. No tecp/** package persistence change, no migration 056/057, no backend, MCP, worker, multi-Cursor, deploy or Production mutation.

Owner decision OD-DLP002-R5. PostgreSQL must be a fresh local ephemeral cluster created only with initdb/pg_ctl, listen_addresses empty, Unix-domain socket only. No TCP listener, environment DATABASE_URL, existing application database, remote/staging/development/production database, Docker/remote fallback, credential read or external API. If local PostgreSQL binaries or isolation proof are unavailable, report BLOCKED and stop.

Owner decision OD-DLP002-R6. Required tests: frozen DLP-001 public-API regression compatibility; caller-owned in-transaction lease mutate without inner BEGIN/COMMIT/ROLLBACK; Task+Claim+Lease one-transaction commit; DENY/failure rolls back all three; two and ten-plus contenders yield exactly one committed owner; idempotent replay and conflicting-key DENY; stale fencing epoch DENY; foreign actor DENY; mid-transaction rollback with no ghost state; database outage fail-closed; invalid governance revision DENY. All failures fail closed.

Owner decision OD-DLP002-R7. The proof remains disposable test evidence only and NON_OPERATIONAL. It is not a real Cursor execution capability, trusted Worker authentication surface, MCP Task/Claim/Release action tool, multi-Cursor pilot, management dashboard, or production control-plane readiness. Immutable durable audit beyond this composition, canonical schema adoption and single-Cursor E2E remain separate future owner decisions.

Owner decision OD-DLP002-R8. After implementation, the exact five-path diff, disposable database isolation, concurrency/fencing/composition logs, focused tests, full frozen TECP regression, Tier 3 security review and owner Human QA must pass on the exact commit. A separate governance closeout must consume this authorization. No CI PASS is presumed. Artemis PROJECT_PROGRESS, Stage 11 progress and STAGE11_IMPLEMENTATION_AUTHORIZED remain unchanged by this TECP slice.

Owner decision OD-DLP002-CLOSEOUT. Formal closeout after PR #235 merge (`b40dcabc036699d07c9abeb513455de5db8d0c0a`) and implementation commit `0d9c8e76f58f835c587c42db38a368b854996029`. Authorization from governance PR #234 is CONSUMED / NON-ACTIVE. Limited Human QA accepted the exact five approved SHA256 hashes. Local evidence: focused 44/44 PASS and frozen TECP 560/560 PASS (NOT GitHub CI). B1 nested-transaction remediation verified. Accepted residual risks R1–R5 remain documented and unresolved. Proof remains NON_OPERATIONAL. No trusted Worker, MCP task actions, production database, deploy or multi-Cursor execution is authorized. No next TECP slice is authorized until a separate owner governance decision.

